 61CR c  {+61}Cr beam produced from fission of a thick uranium carbide          
 61CR2c  target by 1.4 GeV protons.  Cr atoms were ionized using RILIS,         
 61CR3c  then accelerated to 30 keV and mass selected using a high-resolution   
 61CR4c  separator.  Beam was cooled and bunched in a gas-filled                
 61CR5c  linear Paul trap then sent to the Collinear Resonance Ionization       
 61CR6c  Spectroscopy (CRIS) beamline. Measured hyperfine spectra.              
 61CR7c  Deduced ground state J and magnetic dipole moment.                     
 61CR8c  Comparison to large scale shell model calculations and                 
 61CR9c  discrete non-orthogonal shell model calculations.                      
 61CR c  Possible presence of 9/2 isomeric state in {+61}Cr was not             
 61CR2c  observed in the measurement.                                           
